reviews.review:
AMBIANCE: Billy Joel circa Christie Brinkley--a little throwback, a little corny (we heard the same Italian song--the same one they play at the Mets games--3x during our dinner)
PRICE: About 3x what you'd pay anywhere else;
SERVICE: Old school italian joint service and friendliness, Italian love--but watch out, they will use every opportunity to up-charge you even if they are just trying to accommodate you;
FOOD: Mario Batali meets Italian grandmother meets Paula Deen (delicious, more basic but deep flavors, and a TON of butter)
OVERALL: Great for special occasions but way expensive for a "dinner out" (4 of us was $800 with tip); make sure you get that buttery deliciousness of tortellini al ragu; we thought the meatballs were far over-rated
